980	     * {@code postcode} (a present, exact match) yet a <em>different</em> {@code identityKey} - the
981	     * soft-match now keys on the surname sound and postcode rather than an exact last name, and fires
982	     * precisely for the near-miss the identity key lets through (same household surname and postcode
983	     * but a different telephone, so a different key). When such an owner exists,
984	     * {@code possibleDuplicate} is set to {@code true} and {@code possibleDuplicateOf} to that owner's
985	     * id (the lowest id when several match); otherwise {@code possibleDuplicate} is {@code false} and
986	     * {@code possibleDuplicateOf} is left {@code null}. Computed before the new owner is persisted, so
987	     * it considers only the pre-existing owners.
